Suggested attribution
---------------------
"LMEIC derived benchmark data" by Yan, Hu and co-authors, from
https://github.com/lmeic-research/LMEIC, licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Please also cite the paper (see CITATION.cff).

Upstream sources and attribution
--------------------------------
Enron benchmark (data/enron/)
  Derived from the Enron email corpus (Klimt and Yang, 2004; CMU distribution,
  https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~enron/). The corpus is not redistributed here and remains under its
  original terms (research use). The data in data/enron/ contain identifiers, labels, features
  and descriptors derived from it, and no email text, subjects or addresses.

Apache Jira benchmark (data/jira/)
  Derived from the Apache Jira issue-tracking dataset of Diamantopoulos, Nastos and Symeonidis
  (MSR 2023), Zenodo, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14253918,
  licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Changes: we selected 29,997 issues, mapped the creation-time priority to three classes,
  assigned a time-based split, computed context features, and extracted LLM descriptors from the
  issue text. Issue text is not redistributed; rebuild it from the Zenodo dump. The upstream
  attribution and licence of the original dataset apply to everything derived from it.

